content:
zoe: FYI I built a tiny sample app to reproduce a dup POST edge with our Kotlin SDK. It only takes a background cancel + network delay. Hoping we can include it in the SDK repo for CI.

arjun: nice. Is the dup coming from our retry helper or from an auth refresh race?

zoe: looks like both can trigger it but the primary root cause is our execute() -> catch -> clone().execute() pattern. When a coroutine gets cancelled mid-execute the clone path still sends a fresh POST. Repro steps in sample: 1) run SampleActivity 2) hit Send 3) quickly press Home to cancel scope 4) emulate slow network with `adb shell network delay tcp:3000` -> server sometimes sees two /payments POSTs.

pat: can you paste the helper?

zoe:```kotlin
suspend fun safeSend(call: Call): Response = withContext(Dispatchers.IO) {
  try { return@withContext call.execute() }
  catch (e: IOException) { return@withContext call.clone().execute() }
}
```

qa-lee: reproducible rate? customer impact?

zoe: ~10% on emulator under shaped network. One support ticket reported duplicate charges. Low frequency but unacceptable for money endpoints.

arjun: short mitigation: 1) stop auto-retries for non-idempotent verbs unless an Idempotency-Key header exists, 2) add telemetry when a retry would have happened, 3) ship the sample app so QA can fuzz on device farms.

pat: long-term change: replace blocking execute helper with cancellable enqueue wrapper so cancellation propagates to Call:```kotlin
suspend fun Call.awaitCancellable(): Response = suspendCancellableCoroutine { cont ->
  enqueue(object: Callback { override fun onFailure(c: Call, e: IOException) { if(!cont.isCancelled) cont.resumeWithException(e) }
    override fun onResponse(c: Call, r: Response) { if(!cont.isCancelled) cont.resume(r) }
  })
  cont.invokeOnCancellation { cancel() }
}
```

zoe: I wired that into the sample and dups dropped to 0/1000 runs. Also added a tiny README with adb commands so engineers can reproduce locally. I'll open a PR that: removes naive clone retry from core, adds idempotency guard/telemetry, replaces helper with cancellable wrapper, and adds the sample to /samples/android.

sdk-ci: created ticket SDK-6210 and scheduled emulator fuzz job (1000 iterations) to validate.

qa-lee: will run the job and post results. If pass rate is high we can include change in next patch release.

arjun: also add a short note in migration guide about interceptor-based sync refresh causing parity issues when used with suspend adapters. Good work.
